{"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" turns persistence into a declare-and-register concern. You annotate a domain entity with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the macro generates its SwiftData ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" “shadow” class, the value↔model converters, and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistableEntity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance. A generic ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" actor and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" build the container, synthesize one ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" per registered ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":", and reuse the core ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"text":" for debounced, batched writes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Your reducers mutate plain value-type entities inside an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":"; the plugin observes the changelog and writes through to SwiftData after a debounce. Reads happen once, at launch, into memory — the in-memory ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" is the source of truth.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"For low-level manual wiring (writing your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"reference"},{"text":". For the macro details, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","type":"reference"},{"text":". To add cross-device iCloud sync on top, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Before-you-start","level":2,"text":"Before you start","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes a Swidux app already exists — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are wired and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If not, follow ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"reference"},{"text":" first.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a local-only persistence layer. It needs ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no iCloud, CloudKit, or Push entitlements"}]},{"text":" — only the sandbox ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.apple.security.network.client","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entitlement if your app also makes network calls (killswitch, analytics, feature flags). Adding sync entitlements to a local-only app is dead configuration and an App Review risk.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","level":2,"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product to your app target in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPersistence\",","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"Step 2: Annotate your domain entity with `@Persisted`","level":2,"anchor":"Step-2-Annotate-your-domain-entity-with-Persisted","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A persisted entity is a value type that already satisfies ","type":"text"},{"code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"ID == UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" contract). Add ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","    var createdAt: Date","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This generates a ","type":"text"},{"code":"CardModel: @Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" class with ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"toDomain()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"update(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", plus ","type":"text"},{"code":"extension Card: PersistableEntity { typealias Model = CardModel }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". By default every stored property is mirrored directly onto the model — SwiftData persists scalars ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" composites natively, so no manual blob columns are needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated model is "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"CloudKit-safe by construction","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" model backs both the local and the synced container (see "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"reference"},{"text":"). SwiftData’s CloudKit mirroring requires every non-optional attribute to be optional or carry a default value, and every relationship to be optional — validated when the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ModelContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is created. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" satisfies this automatically:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Non-optional mirrored attributes get a default.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If you wrote one on the domain property ("},{"code":"var count: Int = 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), it is propagated verbatim; otherwise the macro fills a canonical default for the known SwiftData primitives ("},{"code":"String → \"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Bool → false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", integers\/floats "},{"code":"→ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Date → .distantPast","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Data → Data()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"UUID → UUID()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Defaults are inert locally — ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overwrites them on every load.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-primitive, non-optional properties"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (a custom ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type, ","type":"text"},{"code":"URL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an enum) have no default the macro can invent. Give the property a default (","type":"text"},{"code":"= …","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), make it optional, or mark it ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — otherwise ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" emits a compile-time error.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Relationships are generated optional"}]},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"var tags: [TagModel]? = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); a non-optional to-one ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a compile-time error (CloudKit forbids non-optional relationships).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" blob columns"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" default to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type is CloudKit-safe through ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Because ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is never decodable, a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"non-optional","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" property must also carry a domain default (","type":"text"},{"code":"= …","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") — the generated getter falls back to it when the blob is missing or undecodable (e.g. a row CloudKit materialized before the blob synced). Omitting the default is a compile-time error (","type":"text"},{"code":"inlineRequiresDefault","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" lives on the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"entity"}]},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"text":" lives on ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state containers","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" slices). They are different layers and never apply to the same type.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Marker macros for non-trivial properties","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Marker-macros-for-non-trivial-properties"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro can’t infer relationships, foreign keys, or which fields are derived. Four property markers (named to avoid SwiftData’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relationship"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"@Transient","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") tell ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":" what to do:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","","    @Inline var styling: TextStyling = TextStyling()  \/\/ one opaque JSON Data column","    @ForeignKey var deckID: UUID                      \/\/ scalar parent reference","    @Relation(deleteRule: .cascade, inverse: \\TagModel.card)","    var tags: [Tag]                                   \/\/ SwiftData relationship","    @Ignored var renderedPreview: String?             \/\/ derived; omitted from the model","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Marker","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effect","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(none)"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mirror the property directly (SwiftData persists scalars and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" composites).","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Force a "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value into a single JSON "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" column (keeps a CloudKit record compact; sidesteps SwiftData "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-attribute edge cases)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@ForeignKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intent marker on a "},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; functionally a mirrored scalar column."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Relation(deleteRule:inverse:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A SwiftData relationship to another ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entity. The property’s type references the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"domain","type":"text"}]},{"text":" type (","type":"text"},{"code":"[Tag]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tag?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Tag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); the model substitutes the ","type":"text"},{"code":"…Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow. "},{"code":"inverse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a key path on the generated model, e.g. "},{"code":"\\TagModel.card","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"deleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"code":"SwiduxDeleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":".cascade","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".nullify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".noAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".deny","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Ignored","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exclude a derived\/denormalized property. Must be optional so it can be reconstructed as "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on load."}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does not generate an "},{"code":"@Attribute(.unique)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — CloudKit forbids unique constraints — so the same generated model works for both local and synced containers. The cost is that rows sharing an "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are possible. "},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles them by converging rather than by assuming uniqueness: writes update every matching row, deletions remove every matching row, and "},{"code":"fetchAll","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" collapses to one value per "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Nothing deletes a duplicate as a side effect of a write."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The one attribute it "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" generate is "},{"code":"@Attribute(.preserveValueOnDeletion)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", on "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and nothing else, so that a deleted row’s identity survives into persistent history where a peer device can read it. It needs no migration: the option leaves the entity’s version hash alone, so stores written before it existed reopen unchanged."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"anchor":"Step-3-Put-the-EntityStore-on-your-state","level":2,"text":"Step 3: Put the `EntityStore` on your state","type":"heading"},{"code":["@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    var cards: EntityStore<Card> = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Your reducers mutate ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.cards","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" like any "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"state.cards[card.id] = card","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"state.cards.modify(id) { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"state.cards[id] = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Every change is recorded for the plugin to drain."}]},{"level":2,"text":"Step 4: Build the coordinator and register the plugin","anchor":"Step-4-Build-the-coordinator-and-register-the-plugin","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", build a local container, create a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", register its plugin, and run first-load hydration before constructing the store:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured() async -> AppStore {","        let container = try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","","        let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","            entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","            container: container,","            debounce: .milliseconds(250)","        )","","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","        \/\/ Register UndoPlugin first if you use it — snapshots must precede writes.","        plugins.register(persistence.corePlugin)","","        var initial = AppState()","        await persistence.hydrate(into: &initial)   \/\/ first-load: fill EntityStores from disk","","        return Store(initialState: initial, reducer: { … }, plugins: plugins)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"hydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first-load only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — it replaces each "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" with the on-disk rows before any live edits exist. It takes "},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" because it runs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before the store is built"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so there is nothing to race with."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The only refresh path after launch is ","type":"text"},{"code":"rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reconciles"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rather than replaces: rows on disk are authoritative except for IDs that still carry unflushed local intent, which always win. So a “refresh from disk” can never clobber pending writes or in-progress UI edits, while remote edits and deletions still surface mid-session. Pass "},{"code":"policy:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — or register an entity with "},{"code":"policy:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — to narrow that; see "},{"code":"MergePolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It takes the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"store","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": re-hydration is asynchronous, and a caller holding a state snapshot across those "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s would discard everything dispatched while they were in flight. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" if edits are vanishing after a load."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need to ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"read","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" rows without touching state, don’t re-hydrate into a throwaway ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — that idiom breaks silently the moment re-hydration starts reading the state it is handed. Use "},{"code":"fetchAll(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"snapshot(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the coordinator instead."}]},{"text":"Reading rows without touching state","type":"heading","anchor":"Reading-rows-without-touching-state","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For exports, migrations, diagnostics, or any other “what’s actually on disk?” question, read directly — naming your domain type, not its generated shadow:"}]},{"code":["let notes = try await persistence.fetchAll(of: Note.self)","let store = try await persistence.snapshot(of: Note.self)   \/\/ as an EntityStore"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both flush the debounce window first by default, so they can’t return a stale row for something the user just edited; pass "},{"code":"flushPending: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on a hot path where that doesn’t matter. Both report failures to "},{"code":"onFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rethrow — there is no state to leave untouched here, so swallowing the error could only present an unreadable database as “no data”."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The entity does not have to be registered with the coordinator; reading a model that is in the container’s schema but not mirrored into state is fine.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Don’t answer these questions by re-hydrating into a throwaway "},{"code":"AppState()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". That reads like a pure fetch but is really a merge, and it breaks silently the moment re-hydration starts consulting the state it is handed."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"important"},{"anchor":"Surfacing-failures","level":3,"text":"Surfacing failures","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every save and fetch failure is logged, and the coordinator accepts an optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"onFailure:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" handler to additionally surface it to your app (a failed ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"save"}]},{"text":" means the in-memory data is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" on disk; a failed ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hydrate fetch"}]},{"text":" leaves that ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntityStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" untouched rather than presenting an unreadable store as “no data”):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","    container: container,","    onFailure: { failure in","        guard failure.isFinal else { return }   \/\/ earlier attempts may still succeed","        \/\/ e.g. dispatch an action that shows a \"couldn't save\" banner","    }",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Retrying-a-failed-save","level":3,"text":"Retrying a failed save","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A flush clears its buffers before the save runs, so a save that fails has nothing left to retry it — the write would reach disk only if the user happened to touch the same entity again. That is silent data loss, so the stack retries.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A failed batch goes ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"back"}]},{"text":" into the writer’s pending buffers, never over anything newer: a later edit to the same entity supersedes the restored value, and a deletion drained while the save was in flight cancels it. ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistencePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" then re-attempts on a doubling backoff, independently of the debounce timer — a write has to land even if the user never touches the app again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Retrying is bounded, because a write that can ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never"}]},{"text":" succeed (disk full, a model the container can’t encode) must not keep the stack busy forever. Tune it with ","type":"text"},{"code":"retry:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","    container: container,","    retry: RetryPolicy(maxAttempts: 5, baseDelay: .milliseconds(500), maxDelay: .seconds(30)),","    onFailure: { failure in ... }",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"RetryPolicy.default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is that policy — five attempts over roughly seven seconds. ","type":"text"},{"code":"RetryPolicy.never","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" opts out of retrying without opting back into losing the write.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the budget runs out you get one final ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistenceFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"isFinal == true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". That is the one worth telling the user about: everything before it was “we’ll try again”. The batch is ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"text":" discarded — it stays pending, so the next edit or an explicit ","type":"text"},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" tries once more, and until then those IDs stay locally owned so a re-hydration can’t overwrite them with the stale stored row.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every attempt is reported, so a handler that shows UI should gate on "},{"code":"isFinal","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Most "},{"code":".save","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" failures are transient and are followed by a success the app never hears about."}]}],"type":"aside","style":"note"},{"anchor":"Diagnostics-what-isnt-a-failure","level":3,"text":"Diagnostics: what isn’t a failure","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Some conditions are worth acting on but aren’t errors, so routing them through ","type":"text"},{"code":"onFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would be wrong. Duplicate rows are the clearest case: CloudKit forbids unique constraints, so several rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are a legitimate on-disk state, not a fault. They go to ","type":"text"},{"code":"onDiagnostic:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards, collapse: EntityCollapse.byID { $0.updatedAt >= $1.updatedAt ? $0 : $1 })],","    container: container,","    onDiagnostic: { diagnostic in","        guard diagnostic.kind == .duplicateRowsCollapsed,","              let count = diagnostic.duplicateCount else { return }","        store.send(.offerDuplicateCleanup(count: count))","    }",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Four kinds ship today:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Kind"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Means"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Payload"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".duplicateRowsCollapsed"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A read found rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Without a ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" resolver they are harmless but permanent — this is what lets you ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"offer","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" the cleanup.","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"entityType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"duplicateCount","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".possibleDispatchLoop"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"text":" fired far more often in one debounce interval than a user could cause. Usually an effect or plugin dispatching on every state change. Reported once per burst, not once per dispatch.","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"drainCount","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".writesUnpersisted","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The set of IDs whose last flush failed changed. Fires again with an "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"empty"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" set once they land, so an indicator can be cleared rather than guessed at."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"entityType","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"unpersistedIDs","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":".mergeWithheld","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A re-hydration left a stored value unapplied because an editing hold was in force. Expected while the user is editing; a hold that outlives the edit shows up here. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"entityType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"withheldIDs","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"PersistenceDiagnostic","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a struct with static constructors rather than an enum, so a future kind can’t break an exhaustive ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in your code — match on ","type":"text"},{"code":"kind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and read the payload you expect. Duplicate reads and dispatch loops are logged whether or not you supply a handler; the unpersisted set has no log of its own, because the individual ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistenceFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s behind it are already logged.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Step 5: Flush on background","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Ste